From: djnice <djnice@freemail.hu>
Subject: openvfd: add the Dune HD Pro 8K Plus display type

The front display of the Dune HD Pro 8K Plus (S928X) is a TM1628 wired as a
common anode panel (transposed: the grids drive the segments, the segment
lines the digits). Its grids carry the segments in the order a, g, b, c, f,
e, d (top, middle, upper right, lower right, upper left, lower left,
bottom), which none of the existing glyph tables matches. Add a table for it
as display type 0x0B; the vendor kernel calls it tm1628 display_type 1.
---
diff --git a/OpenVFDService.c b/OpenVFDService.c
index c0ab7a2..4391675 100644
--- a/OpenVFDService.c
+++ b/OpenVFDService.c
@@ -515,6 +515,9 @@ void select_display_type()
 			case DISPLAY_TYPE_5D_7S_TAP1:
 				ledCodes = LED_decode_tab5;
 				break;
+			case DISPLAY_TYPE_5D_7S_DUNE:
+				ledCodes = LED_decode_tab6;
+				break;
 			default:
 				ledCodes = LED_decode_tab2;
 				break;
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index f208e97..c9d1070 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@ This repository contains the Linux kernel driver and userspace service for FD628
 | `0x08` | 4D_7S_FREESATGTC | Freesat GTC |
 | `0x09` | 5D_7S_TAP1 | TAP1 |
 | `0x0A` | 5D_X96_X9 | X96/X9 |
+| `0x0B` | 5D_7S_DUNE | Dune HD Pro 8K Plus |
 
 ### Display Modes
 
@@ -166,6 +167,7 @@ vfd_display_type='0x01,0x00,0x00,0x00'  # type,reserved,flags,controller
 | `0x08` | 4D_7S_FREESATGTC | Freesat GTC |
 | `0x09` | 5D_7S_TAP1 | TAP1 |
 | `0x0A` | 5D_X96_X9 | X96/X9 |
+| `0x0B` | 5D_7S_DUNE | Dune HD Pro 8K Plus |
 
 ### 显示模式
 
